{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G7.DATA_H.DATA_HANDLING",
 "title": "Data Handling",
 "status": "draft: written 17 Nov 2026 offline for the Grade 7 pilot; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to k are tested; l is an attitude. Data and its collection (a, b); frequency tables from tallies, with totals, missing frequencies, the most common value and percentages (c); a suitable scale for a bar graph and the value of a pictograph symbol (d); pictographs (e); drawing and reading bar graphs (f, g); drawing pie charts from angles that make 360 and reading them as shares of their own total (h, i); line graphs and reading between points (j); travel graphs: stops, the speed of each part, the average speed with the stop, and where two lines cross (k). Choosing the right graph for the data is filed under f, h and j. Grade 5 tallied and made frequency tables; Grade 6 drew pictographs and bar graphs. The older families were filed under letters from an earlier draft: the pictograph family is filed under e, bar-reading under g, pie-reading under i.",
 "skills": [
  {
   "skill": "MATH.G7.DATA_H.DATA_HANDLING.DATA_MEANING_COLLECT",
